<title>USA: US Justice says FMC settles military claims.</title>
<headline>US Justice says FMC settles military claims.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Justice Department said Tuesday that FMC Corp will pay $13 million to settle claims it falsely inflated the cost of Army contracts for tanks and the Bradley Fighting Vehicle.</p>
<p>It said the settlement resolved allegations filed in a complaint under the so-called whistleblower law by a former manager at FMC's Ground Systems Division in San Jose, California.</p>
<p>The civil lawsuit had charged FMC falsely inflated the amount it intended to spend on independent research and development, and bid and proposal projects in 1991 and 1992, the department said.</p>
</text>
